# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# VITE_ vars are inlined into the public JS bundle at build time. This value is
# visible to anyone who opens the app — it is NOT a secret and NOT an
# authorization boundary. Its only job is to stop a worker who picks up the
# shared tablet from cutting stock with one stray tap.
#
# Real authorization is Firebase Auth + firestore.rules (deny-by-default,
# staff-email only). If you leave this unset, editor mode still works for the
# staff account signed in via Firebase Auth; the password prompt simply becomes
# unavailable for everyone else. That is the safer default.
VITE_OPERATOR_PASSWORD=